
v0.3.1:
 - BUG FIX: an empty daemon group uses `_.sock` as the control socket
 - BUG FIX: on Windows, another control client can connect while one connection is still open
 - BUG FIX: a relative pid file is created in the working directory from before daemonizing, and the lock is held until the process exits
 - BUG FIX: `--panic-quit` in monitored mode still shuts the process down after notifying the parent
 - BUG FIX: a non-ASCII size string in config is rejected instead of panicking
 - BUG FIX: the Windows hostname sent to syslog no longer includes a trailing NUL
 - Compatibility: DragonFly worker `sched_affinity` applies to the calling thread

v0.3.0:
 - Breaking: graphite exporter always writes the cumulative counter sum and no longer accepts `counter_value`
 - Feature: prometheus_push exporter pushes cumulative counters and gauges with Prometheus remote write 1.0
 - Feature: HTTP exporters (`opentsdb`, `influxdb_v2`, `influxdb_v3`, `prometheus_push`) close the connection after `idle_timeout` (default 45s); the next batch opens a new connection
 - Feature: optional snmalloc global allocator at compile time; `--version -v` reports `snmalloc`
 - Feature: publish Debian and Alpine container images that listen on `0.0.0.0:8125` and print aggregated metrics to stdout
 - Feature: deb, rpm, and container image builds accept an optional Rust PGO profile
 - Compatibility: default deb/rpm package builds use secure-snmalloc
 - Compatibility: macOS stays in the foreground after libc removed `daemon()`
 - Compatibility: replace chrono with jiff for timestamps
 - Compatibility: bump MSRV to 1.95.0

v0.2.0:
 - BUG FIX: scale statsd counters by `1/sample_rate` when `|@rate` is present so sampled metrics are not under-counted (gauges stay absolute)
 - BUG FIX: exporter aggregate `diff` resets per emit interval instead of being overwritten, so interval counters and rates are correct
 - Feature: graphite exporter `counter_value` (`sum` | `diff`) chooses lifetime total vs emit-interval delta; default remains `sum` for existing dashboards
 - Feature: reload the running process via RPC/ctl (`reload`) without a full restart
 - Feature: optional jemalloc or mimalloc global allocator at compile time; allocator name/version appear in `--version`
 - Feature: derive default config / log / metrics / controller names from the binary name (supports renamed installs)
 - Compatibility: bump MSRV to 1.91.0

v0.1.1:
 - Feature: statsd importer can listen on a Unix datagram socket in addition to UDP
 - Feature: allow to set hop_limit and traffic_class ipv6 socket options

v0.1.0:
 - Initial release
